From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 11:37:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] net: stmmac: meson8b: reset the MAC after a WoL resume

On S4 (dwmac 3.70a, internal RMII PHY), RX and TX stall after a resume
from the WoL power-down mode in about 60% of cycles. Only a full close
and open recovers the MAC. Request a reset after a WoL resume.

Signed-off-by: Igor Pecovnik <igor@armbian.com>
---
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c | 2 ++
 drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c   | 4 ++++
 include/linux/stmmac.h                              | 1 +
 3 files changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c
index e4d5c41294f4..3f730023b232 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/dwmac-meson8b.c
@@ -460,6 +460,8 @@ static int meson8b_dwmac_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		return ret;
 
 	plat_dat->bsp_priv = dwmac;
+	/* The MAC can stall after a WoL resume until the next open */
+	plat_dat->flags |= STMMAC_FLAG_RESET_AFTER_WOL;
 
 	return stmmac_dvr_probe(&pdev->dev, plat_dat, &stmmac_res);
 }
diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
index b837e8e27a35..8ff11527d8fe 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/stmicro/stmmac/stmmac_main.c
@@ -8393,6 +8393,10 @@ int stmmac_resume(struct device *dev)
 
 	netif_device_attach(ndev);
 
+	/* Some MACs stall after the WoL power-down mode. Reset them. */
+	if (priv->wolopts && (priv->plat->flags & STMMAC_FLAG_RESET_AFTER_WOL))
+		stmmac_global_err(priv);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_GPL(stmmac_resume);
diff --git a/include/linux/stmmac.h b/include/linux/stmmac.h
index 4430b967abde..243427e7f6d4 100644
--- a/include/linux/stmmac.h
+++ b/include/linux/stmmac.h
@@ -211,6 +211,7 @@ enum dwmac_core_type {
 #define STMMAC_FLAG_HWTSTAMP_CORRECT_LATENCY	BIT(14)
 #define STMMAC_FLAG_KEEP_PREAMBLE_BEFORE_SFD	BIT(15)
 #define STMMAC_FLAG_SERDES_SUPPORTS_2500M	BIT(16)
+#define STMMAC_FLAG_RESET_AFTER_WOL		BIT(17)
 
 struct mac_device_info;
 
